<section class="section">

<h2>The Proposed Solution</h2>

<p>
Dual Brain Robotics introduces a framework in which autonomous
systems process information through interacting cognitive channels
rather than a single decision stream.
</p>

</section>

<section class="section">

<h2>Research Foundation</h2>

<p>
The architecture emerges from decades of work in social psychology,
perception theory, autism research, and the study of consciousness.
</p>

</section>

<section class="section">

<h2>Potential Applications</h2>

<ul>
<li>Autonomous Robotics</li>
<li>Human-Robot Interaction</li>
<li>Adaptive Learning Systems</li>
<li>Assistive Technologies</li>
<li>Cognitive Architecture Research</li>
<li>Consciousness Studies</li>
</ul>

</section>

